  "result": "Perfect! All 101 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT calculations:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n\u2705 **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added VAT functionality:\n- `lineVat(line)` function: Calculates VAT on line amount after discount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) * vatRate / 100`, rounded and clamped at 0\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where:\n  - VAT = sum of all line VATs (per-line VAT is rounded, then summed)\n  - total = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n\u2705 **src/render.js** \u2014 Updated to display VAT:\n- Shows \"VAT: \u20acX.XX\" line only when VAT > 0\n- VAT line appears just above the total line\n- Maintains clean output for VAT-exempt invoices\n\n\u2705 **test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 Added 8 comprehensive VAT tests:\n- `lineVat` calculations with different rates and discounts\n- VAT with fractional cent rounding\n- Invoice VAT as sum of line VATs\n- Total calculation including VAT\n- All tests verify integer results\n\n\u2705 **test/render.test.js** \u2014 Added VAT rendering tests:\n- Verifies VAT line displays when non-zero\n- Verifies VAT line hidden when zero\n- Tests correct VAT amount display\n\n**Key design:**\n- VAT is calculated per line on the amount **after discount**, not on the line total\n- Each line's VAT is rounded independently, then summed for the invoice VAT\n- Invoice total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat` (all clamped at 0)\n- VAT display is conditional\u2014only shown when there's actual VAT to display",
